Validate ImageCmsTransform.apply() input/output modes (CVE-2026-59205)

Pillow before 12.3.0 only checked the output mode in apply_in_place().
Calling ImageCmsTransform.apply(im, imOut) with an output image whose mode
does not match the transform's declared output mode can trigger a controlled
native heap out-of-bounds write. Validate both input and output modes in
apply(), and route apply_in_place() through that check.

Upstream fix: https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/a9ffc42 (PR #9698)

